"The north child is Eira, Tygryth's frost-white daughter, taken the same night as Aeron."
"The keepers held Eira two hundred years in their house at the heart of the northern peaks."
"The keepers took Eira's young from her there and sold them downriver."
"A hundred years ago Eira broke her iron, killed her keepers, and sealed herself under the ice."
"Eira sleeps so as not to feel the loss of her young; she is alive."
"Eira's ice opens only to the kin-fire her mother lit."
"The bronze map is the keepers' survey of Eira's house; its undrawn centre is her ice."
"No keeper who went into the centre of the ringed peaks came out, so none drew it."
